WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.535
Mary knew she had to answer Colin's questions about the secret garden, but she didn't want to.

2
00:00:08.536 --> 00:00:13.658
"Your father hated the garden. He locked the door," she said nervously.

3
00:00:13.659 --> 00:00:16.509
"No one knew where he buried the key."

4
00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:21.058
"What sort of garden is it?" Colin asked eagerly.

5
00:00:21.059 --> 00:00:26.702
"No one has been allowed to go inside for ten years," Mary said carefully.

6
00:00:26.703 --> 00:00:31.503
But it was too late to be careful. Colin was just like Mary.

7
00:00:31.504 --> 00:00:34.668
He'd had nothing to think about for years.

8
00:00:34.669 --> 00:00:40.517
So the idea of a hidden garden interested him, just as it had interested her.

9
00:00:40.518 --> 00:00:44.866
He asked question after question. Where was it?

10
00:00:44.867 --> 00:00:49.119
Had she looked for the door? Had she asked the gardeners?

11
00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:53.946
"I think they've been told not to answer questions about it," said Mary.

12
00:00:53.947 --> 00:00:56.358
"I would make them answer."

13
00:00:56.359 --> 00:01:00.023
"You would?" Mary began to feel frightened.

14
00:01:00.024 --> 00:01:04.742
If Colin could force people to answer, who knew what might happen!

15
00:01:04.743 --> 00:01:08.074
"I told you that everyone must please me.

16
00:01:08.075 --> 00:01:13.443
If I were to live, this place would someday belong to me. They all know that."

17
00:01:13.444 --> 00:01:17.387
In the past people had said that Mary was spoiled.

18
00:01:17.388 --> 00:01:20.241
She had never seen this in herself.

19
00:01:20.242 --> 00:01:23.849
But now she could see it quite plainly in Colin.

20
00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:27.121
He thought the whole world belonged to him.

21
00:01:27.122 --> 00:01:32.094
How mysterious he was and how coolly he spoke about dying.

22
00:01:32.095 --> 00:01:35.072
"Do you really think you're going to die?"

23
00:01:35.073 --> 00:01:41.111
Mary was curious about this, but she also wanted to distract him from the garden.

24
00:01:41.112 --> 00:01:44.651
"That's what people have been saying for a long time.

25
00:01:44.652 --> 00:01:48.644
My doctor is my father's cousin. He's quite poor.

26
00:01:48.645 --> 00:01:53.452
If I die, he'll have Misselthwaite Manor when my father is dead.

27
00:01:53.453 --> 00:01:56.042
I don't think he wants me to live."

28
00:01:56.043 --> 00:01:58.628
"Do you want to live?"

29
00:01:58.629 --> 00:02:04.386
"No." Colin sounded tired and angry. "But I don't want to die.

30
00:02:04.387 --> 00:02:08.755
When I'm ill, I lie here and think about dying until I cry."

31
00:02:08.756 --> 00:02:11.870
"I've heard you crying three times."

32
00:02:11.871 --> 00:02:14.080
"Let's talk about something else.

33
00:02:14.081 --> 00:02:17.582
Let's talk about that garden. Don't you want to see it?"

34
00:02:17.583 --> 00:02:20.735
"Yes," Mary said.

35
00:02:20.736 --> 00:02:25.540
"I want the key dug up. I'm going to make the servants open the door.

36
00:02:25.541 --> 00:02:30.405
I'll make them take me there in my wheelchair. And I will let you come too."

37
00:02:30.406 --> 00:02:35.737
Mary clutched her hands tightly. Everything would be ruined—everything!

38
00:02:35.738 --> 00:02:38.076
Dickon would never come back.

39
00:02:38.077 --> 00:02:42.513
She would never again feel as safe as a bird on her nest.

40
00:02:42.514 --> 00:02:46.234
"Oh, don't do that!" she cried.

41
00:02:46.235 --> 00:02:49.559
Colin stared at her. "Why?"

42
00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:53.619
"If you make them take you there, it'll never be a secret again.

43
00:02:53.620 --> 00:03:00.413
You see, if no one knows but us, and if we could find the hidden door, we could slip through it together."

44
00:03:00.414 --> 00:03:03.991
Mary's words came tumbling out.

45
00:03:03.992 --> 00:03:08.706
"We could play there every day and pretend we're birds and it's our nest.

46
00:03:08.707 --> 00:03:13.942
We could watch the flowers growing in the spring and see how many roses are alive.

47
00:03:13.943 --> 00:03:17.546
Don't you see how much nicer it would be if it were a secret?"

48
00:03:17.547 --> 00:03:23.986
There was an odd expression on his face. "I've never had a secret before."

49
00:03:23.987 --> 00:03:26.480
"Perhaps I could find the door.

50
00:03:26.481 --> 00:03:30.153
Then we could find some boy to take you out in your wheelchair."

51
00:03:30.154 --> 00:03:33.004
"I wouldn't mind fresh air in a secret garden."

52
00:03:33.005 --> 00:03:37.974
Colin suddenly looked pleased. "I'm going to show you something.

53
00:03:37.975 --> 00:03:43.838
Do you see that curtain hanging above the fireplace? Open it."

54
00:03:43.839 --> 00:03:46.868
Mary got up and pulled open the curtain.

55
00:03:46.869 --> 00:03:50.535
Underneath was a painting of a beautiful woman.

56
00:03:50.536 --> 00:03:54.524
"That's my mother. Sometimes I hate her for dying.

57
00:03:54.525 --> 00:03:58.668
If she were alive, maybe I wouldn't always be sick.

58
00:03:58.669 --> 00:04:03.248
And my father wouldn't hate to look at me. Draw the curtain again."

59
00:04:03.249 --> 00:04:08.440
Mary noticed that Colin's large, dark eyes were just like his mother's.

60
00:04:08.441 --> 00:04:13.851
She drew the curtain and sat down by the bed. "Why is the curtain closed?"

61
00:04:13.852 --> 00:04:19.058
"I don't like to see her looking at me. She smiles too much when I'm sick.

62
00:04:19.059 --> 00:04:23.487
Besides, she's mine, and I don't want everyone to see her."

63
00:04:23.488 --> 00:04:26.309
They were quiet for a few moments.

64
00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:31.650
"What would Mrs. Medlock do if she found out I was here?" asked Mary.

65
00:04:31.651 --> 00:04:35.734
"She'd do as I say. And I'd tell her that I want you to come every day.

66
00:04:35.735 --> 00:04:37.619
I'm glad you came."

67
00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:40.199
"So am I."

68
00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:43.241
"But for now I think I'll keep you a secret.

69
00:04:43.242 --> 00:04:47.086
I'll tell Martha when I want you to come. Do you know Martha?"

70
00:04:47.087 --> 00:04:53.061
Mary nodded. Now she understood Martha's troubled look when she asked about the crying.

71
00:04:53.062 --> 00:04:56.830
"Martha takes care of me when my nurse has the night off.

72
00:04:56.831 --> 00:05:01.624
She's sleeping in the next room right now." Colin yawned.

73
00:05:01.625 --> 00:05:04.983
"You're tired. I think I'd better go."

74
00:05:04.984 --> 00:05:07.896
"Oh, please don't go until I fall asleep."

75
00:05:07.897 --> 00:05:11.614
Somehow Mary felt sorry for this strange boy.

76
00:05:11.615 --> 00:05:15.476
So she sang softly until he fell asleep.

77
00:05:15.477 --> 00:05:23.391
Then she picked up her candle and crept away.

